      </h2>
      <p>
        When rolling out Nix Flakes across an engineering organization, anticipate and resolve the following 4 common friction points:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-4 text-slate-300">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">1. Untracked Files Not Found by Nix:</strong> Nix Flakes only recognizes files tracked by Git. If you create a new configuration file or script and run <code>nix develop</code> before staging it, Nix throws a <code>file not found</code> error. <em>Remediation:</em> Run <code>git add .</code> so Nix includes the new files in its evaluation sandbox.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">2. Apple Silicon Missing SDK Frameworks:</strong> On macOS, building packages that interact with SSL or networking may fail with <code>framework not found Security</code>. <em>Remediation:</em> Add <code>darwin.apple_sdk.frameworks.Security</code> and <code>darwin.apple_sdk.frameworks.CoreFoundation</code> conditionally under <code>pkgs.stdenv.isDarwin</code> in <code>buildInputs</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">3. Outdated `flake.lock` Dependency Drift:</strong> If different team members run <code>nix flake update</code> independently, your inputs will diverge. <em>Remediation:</em> Commit <code>flake.lock</code> directly into version control and enforce lockfile immutability in CI via <code>nix develop --no-update-lock-file</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">4. Direnv Security Approval Required:</strong> When cloning a new repository, direnv refuses to run unauthorized code until granted permission. <em>Remediation:</em> Instruct new team members to run <code>direnv allow</code> once upon initial project setup.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Frequently Asked Questions: Hermetic Python Environments &amp; Nix Toolchains
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">Why combine Nix Flakes with uv instead of using pure Nix poetry2nix?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Pure Nix Python packaging (poetry2nix/dream2nix) requires rebuilding wheels from source inside the Nix sandbox, which frequently breaks with complex modern C-extensions like PyTorch and Pydantic-Core. Using Nix to provide system C libraries and uv to manage Python wheels delivers sub-second resolution and 100% wheel compatibility.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How does direnv automate Nix Flake shell activation?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            By adding 'use flake' to an authorized .envrc file, direnv automatically evaluates the flake.nix devShell and exports all binary PATHs and environment variables into your terminal session instantly upon cd-ing into the directory.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">Does this setup work across both macOS (Apple Silicon) and Linux?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Yes. Using flake-utils or eachDefaultSystem automatically configures native package outputs for x86_64-linux, aarch64-linux, and aarch64-darwin (Apple Silicon M1-M4) with zero code duplication.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How does Nix resolve missing C-extension headers like libpq-fe.h?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Nix provides exact include directories and shared libraries in buildInputs (e.g. pkgs.postgresql, pkgs.openssl), setting CPATH, LIBRARY_PATH, and LD_LIBRARY_PATH in the shellHook so compilation succeeds deterministically on every machine.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

